WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
You tell a friend a small lie.

2
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:04.990
No one else will ever find out.

3
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.480
Yet a quiet sense of
shame may stay with you.

4
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.850
Most people also believe
some things are really wrong,

5
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.520
not just disliked.

6
00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:17.760
Yet different cultures and ages have
disagreed about what is right and what is

7
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:18.720
wrong.

8
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:24.020
So why do we feel some things are wrong,
even when nobody would ever find out?

9
00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.830
In this mission, you'll
build the moral argument,

10
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.600
one step at a time.

11
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.360
Then you'll set three explanations
of conscience side by side,

12
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.760
and weigh them up.

13
00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:38.560
Your mission: explain why we feel some
things are wrong even when no one would

14
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.390
find out.
